<title>JAPAN: BOXING-YOKTHAI RETAINS BANTAMWEIGHT TITLE.</title>
<headline>BOXING-YOKTHAI RETAINS BANTAMWEIGHT TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>NAGOYA, Japan. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Yokthai Sith Oar retained his World Boxing Association (WBA) junior bantamweight title on Tuesday with a draw against Japanese challenger Satoshi Iida.</p>
<p>It was the third defence Yokthai, who won the title by knocking out Alimi Goitia of Venezuela last August.</p>
<p>The 22-year-old former kick boxer also remained unbeaten at 13-0 with eight knockouts and now one draw.</p>
<p>South Korean judge Park Dong An scored the fight 115-115 and Oswaldo Sanchez of Venezuela had it 114-114. The third judge, Manuel Rodriguez of Colombia, gave the fight to Iida 116-113 but under the bout's rules two judges needed to agree on a winner.</p>
</text>
